From 73322d06cdba957b4eac3b67039e93fb02a26790 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 02:43:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: give the healing-chance adjustments the direction their
 comments state

borg_heal() draws chance = randint0(100) and returns without healing
when chance is below the threshold for how badly hurt the borg is, so a
lower chance means a skip is more likely.  Three adjustments before
that test had the opposite sign to what their comments say:

- "if we are fighting a unique increase the odds of healing" subtracted
  10, making healing less likely next to a unique;
- "if danger is close to the hp and healing will help, do it" subtracted
  75, so a borg whose danger was at or above its current hit points (but
  below its maximum) skipped every healing step whenever it had lost
  less than 75% of its hit points, and three times in four above that;
- "Risky Borgs are less likely to heal in the fight" added 5, making a
  risky borg heal more often.

Flip the three signs.  The class adjustment (-25 for classes other than
priest and paladin, which makes those classes heal less readily) and the
thresholds are unchanged.  A borg that is in real danger and is carrying
something that heals enough now uses it instead of falling through to
escapes such as reading Word of Recall.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#364.

(cherry picked from commit b366550f776d4d7a6ac52031529f3254a5914d38)
---
 src/borg/borg-caution.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-caution.c b/src/borg/borg-caution.c
index 43a99dd0b..038a211e8 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-caution.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-caution.c
@@ -325,11 +325,11 @@ static bool borg_heal(int danger)
 
     /* if we are fighting a unique increase the odds of healing */
     if (borg.near.unique)
-        chance -= 10;
+        chance += 10;
 
     /* if danger is close to the hp and healing will help, do it */
     if (danger >= borg.trait[BI_CURHP] && danger < borg.trait[BI_MAXHP])
-        chance -= 75;
+        chance += 75;
     else {
         if (borg.trait[BI_CLASS] != CLASS_PRIEST
             && borg.trait[BI_CLASS] != CLASS_PALADIN)
@@ -338,7 +338,7 @@ static bool borg_heal(int danger)
 
     /* Risky Borgs are less likely to heal in the fight */
     if (borg_cfg[BORG_PLAYS_RISKY])
-        chance += 5;
+        chance -= 5;
 
     if (((pct_down <= 15 && chance < 98)
             || (pct_down >= 16 && pct_down <= 25 && chance < 95)
